FlorisBoard IME vendored in this module
=======================================

Upstream: https://github.com/florisboard/florisboard
Pinned commit: 2e82060251897226c0739b9f52d1d051b02305fb (tag v0.5.2)
License: Apache License, Version 2.0. The upstream LICENSE is copied verbatim
as android/keyboard/LICENSE.

The Kotlin sources of the upstream :app and :lib:android, :lib:color,
:lib:compose, :lib:kotlin, :lib:native and :lib:snygg modules are merged into
src/main/kotlin; their resources and assets are merged into src/main/res and
src/main/assets. The Rust source of :lib:native is kept under src/main/rust
for provenance but is not compiled: the only native entry point is called from
FlorisApplication.onCreate, and the shell uses its own Application class, so
the JNI library is never loaded in this APK.

JetPref is a separate Apache-2.0 library by Patrick Goldinger
(https://github.com/patrickgold/jetpref). The upstream snapshot dependency no
longer exists, so this build uses the published 0.3.0-beta02 (commit d6e12dda,
2025-11-19), which is the same v3 API as the snapshot.

Local change: `ime/editor/KeyboardDigits.kt` folds every Unicode decimal digit to
ASCII before a key is committed, because this product writes ASCII digits only.
The upstream numeric-row assets stay as published; the fold happens at the
commit boundary, so choosing any of them cannot emit a non-ASCII digit.

Not vendored: the optional full Chinese shape-based language packs documented
in upstream LANGUAGEPACKS-CHINESE.md, which are GPL-3.0. The default barebones
Chinese pack shipped in the upstream assets is Apache-2.0 and is retained.

The AboutLibraries third-party-licenses screen is omitted from the merged
sources: it depends on a Gradle plugin absent from this build and would list
the upstream app's licenses rather than this APK's.
